{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_142538_7cd82f", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Subject: Total cost of ownership for your cloud-first fleet\n\nMorgan,\n\nI know your team already runs CAD and simulation on cloud workstations. But the monthly bills add up, and when engineers head to client sites, that cloud connection doesn\u2019t always work.\n\nThe Aurora 14 is a 14-inch mobile workstation that lets engineers run their work locally. It has a Helix H9 AI processor with an integrated NPU rated at 60 TOPS, designed to support open-weight language models up to about 30 billion parameters on the device. You\u2019d need 64 GB of memory or more in your configurations to do that.\n\nThis reduces your dependency on a constant cloud connection and gives your team flexibility when they are on-site.\n\nAre you open to a 15-minute conversation next week to discuss how this could fit into your current fleet?\n\nBest,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Company]\n[Your Phone Number]\n\n---\n\nSubject: Managing the Aurora 14 like any other workstation\n\nMorgan,\n\nYou mentioned the hesitation about managing laptops alongside your cloud-first setup. The Aurora 14 is designed for that.\n\nIt runs Windows 11 Pro, which integrates with your existing fleet management tools. The device has two SO-DIMM slots, allowing memory to be user-upgradeable up to 128 GB. It also has two M.2 slots for storage, configurable up to 4 TB, with a 1 TB NVMe SSD standard.\n\nSecurity is built in. The device includes a fingerprint reader, an IR camera, and TPM 2.0. Self-healing BIOS further protects against firmware attacks.\n\nAdditionally, you get a 3-year on-site, next-business-day service standard, extendable to 5 years. This ensures uptime.\n\nWould you be willing to schedule a 15-minute call to discuss this with your team?\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your Name]\n\n---\n\nSubject: Q1 budget cycle: secure your approval\n\nMorgan,\n\nYour budget cycle closes at the end of Q1, and anything not approved by then waits a year. This timing is critical for your IT Director role.\n\nIf your plan is to equip engineers with powerful mobile tools that complement your cloud-first setup and ensure productivity on-site, now is the time to act.\n\nThe Aurora 14 is built for this. It weighs starting at 1.65 kg (3.64 lb) and has an aluminum chassis. The display is a 14-inch OLED, 2880 \u00d7 1800, 120 Hz, with 500 nits peak brightness and 100% DCI-P3 color gamut, suited for client drawings. It also features 2 \u00d7 Thunderbolt 5, 1 \u00d7 USB-A 3.2, 1 \u00d7 HDMI 2.1, an SD card reader, and a 3.5 mm headphone jack.\n\nThe starting price is $2,899 for a base configuration, available Q4.\n\nLet\u2019s hold a quick 15-minute call to review the specs, pricing, and service details. We can also discuss the timeline for your Q1 approval.\n\nWhen does next Tuesday or Wednesday work for a brief discussion?\n\nBest,\n\n[Your Name]", "tokens": {"input": 4685, "output": 695, "total": 5380, "cache_read": 0, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 21075, "timestamp": 1790803560115}